Box86 patch 17 -- native Wayland objects for native Vulkan on the RG353VS.

Apply after FINALPLAY15-box86-complete.patch to Box86 commit
0579f8b9c47d87d700724f4cce559b06cbd2b0f5.  The final binary keeps the complete
MGS2 FP15 island/mutex/memmove/DirectSound/dither chain and adds only the
Wayland/Vulkan wrapper delta below.

Why: proprietary armhf libmali is native code.  Its Vulkan WSI entry points
must receive native wl_display / wl_surface objects; forwarding Box86 guest
Wayland objects is an ABI violation.  DXVK cannot create a legal swapchain
without this bridge.

This is a cold/WSI compatibility enabler.  No separate FPS gain is claimed.
The generated wrapper files are included because they are part of the exact
build input, not regenerated implicitly during release reconstruction.

